.TH visor 1  "visor 0.6.0" 
.SH NAME
visor \- Your Visor finances from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvisor\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-space\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Your Visor finances from the terminal
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the API response body as JSON instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-space\fR \fI<SPACE>\fR
Space to act on, by name or ID [default: the one set with `visor spaces use`]
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Print each HTTP request (method, URL, status, time, request ID) on standard error
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
visor\-auth(1)
Log in, log out, and check the stored login
.TP
visor\-whoami(1)
Show who is logged in, how, and the space commands act on
.TP
visor\-doctor(1)
Check the CLI version, the login, and the connection to Visor
.TP
visor\-update(1)
Update the CLI the way it was installed: Homebrew or the installer
.TP
visor\-open(1)
Open Visor in the browser: the dashboard or a page of it
.TP
visor\-me(1)
Show the user the token belongs to
.TP
visor\-spaces(1)
List spaces and choose the default one
.TP
visor\-transactions(1)
List, record, edit, and delete transactions
.TP
visor\-accounts(1)
List accounts
.TP
visor\-categories(1)
List categories
.TP
visor\-tags(1)
List tags
.TP
visor\-cards(1)
List credit cards and their bills
.TP
visor\-subscriptions(1)
List subscriptions
.TP
visor\-fixed\-bills(1)
List fixed bills, such as rent or utilities
.TP
visor\-installments(1)
List installment plans
.TP
visor\-goals(1)
List goals
.TP
visor\-investments(1)
List investments
.TP
visor\-connections(1)
List Open Finance connections and their sync status
.TP
visor\-overview(1)
Show balances, the month so far, and the projection for a space
.TP
visor\-pix(1)
Send a Pix that you confirm with biometrics at your bank (Premium)
.TP
visor\-notifications(1)
List notifications
.TP
visor\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script
.TP
visor\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Authentication:
  Run `visor auth login` to log in through the browser (Pro or Premium
  plan). On a machine without a browser, use a personal API token from
  https://dashboard.visorfinance.app/settings/connected_apps with
  `visor auth login \-\-with\-token`. VISOR_TOKEN overrides the stored login.

Exit codes:
  0 success, 1 failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 not authenticated or not allowed,
  4 not found, 5 request rejected, 6 rate limited or Visor unavailable

Docs: https://docs.visorfinance.app
.SH VERSION
v0.6.0
